# org-target: docs/10-19-design/10-architecture/10.23-native-aitia-backpressure-content-review.org::#cross-owner-history-handover
# render-layout: elk; theme: 0; pad: 24; timeout: 30
direction: down
host: "Trusted host\nPins actual predecessor capability and existing root\nOwner label alone is not source authority"
evidence: "Existing ASCENT source exchanges\n46 real observations / seven counters\nExisting Aitia mechanical requests and repairs"
old: "Old approval owner\nAppend-only complete decision inventory\nFrozen signed bodies + file closure\nExact ordered native cut + parent authority lineage"
grant: "Actual root-signed handover\nFrom + to + technical digest + cut + full ordered IDs\nNo new approval required from old owner"
missing: "Missing / closed old producer\nIncomplete IDs / wrong recipient / stale cut\nSubmission refused or discovery pending\nCopied records are not an archive fallback"
new: "Successor uses existing native Aitia\nSdlcHistorySource: predecessor becomes mandatory\nSdlcHistoryDiscovery: two intakes + predecessor\nSdlcAuthorityAttestation: reverify inherited decisions"
core: "Existing Core receipt owner\nFresh successor-local native requests and receipts\nOld receipt presentations cannot transfer authority\nChanged grant reference invalidates old frame"
gate: "Actual use check\nUnverified mandatory history -> pending\nUnresolved verified rejection -> rejected\nExplicit named authorized resolution -> review admitted\nRelease authority remains false"
change: "Old owner accepts another counter\nEarlier handover cut becomes stale\nExpanded grant + complete reimport + fresh verification\nEarlier resolution does not close the new counter"
reuse: "Reuse boundary\nRetain real method evidence and signed history\nSame owner / cut / bytes / current receipts may reuse\nGrant disappears -> pending; exact restoration may recover"
limits: "Bounded qualification\n16 gold checks in two independent native replays\nLocal test-only signatures and trusted host custody\nNo global reset detection, durable recovery or atomic effect"
host -> old
host -> grant
old -> grant -> new -> core -> gate
evidence -> new
old -> missing
missing -> gate: "no complete discovery"
old -> change -> new: "reopen"
gate -> reuse -> limits
